# Target C support-seven H6: reflection-closure bound

Date: 2026-09-19

Status: exact symmetry/counting reduction inside the generic H6 branch. The theorem-state authority is unchanged. C-II remains open.

## Result

The exact generic-H6 interior-force census contains

\[
14174=10670\,C_7+3504\,(C_3\sqcup C_4)
\]

labelled cells. The current committed exact reductions leave

\[
4805=3823\,C_7+982\,(C_3\sqcup C_4).
\]

The current 4,805-cell ground-pattern census is not invariant under the exact H6 hull reflection. Closing the already-proved exclusions under that reflection forces at least

\[
\boxed{80}
\]

further generic-H6 exclusions. Therefore the reflection-closed generic-H6 survivor set has size at most

\[
\boxed{4725}.
\]

This is a rigorous upper bound, not an exact new survivor census. It uses only the exact 14,174-cell combinatorial universe, the current certified ground-pattern census, and an exact relabeling symmetry. No new floating-point LP output is used.

## Reflection

Use the reciprocal-label involution

\[
\rho=(1\ 5)(2\ 4),
\qquad
\rho(0)=0,\quad \rho(3)=3,\quad \rho(6)=6,\quad \rho(7)=7.
\]

Geometrically this is reflection of the reciprocal hexagonal hull through the axis through hull vertices `0` and `3`, followed by the displayed relabeling. It preserves the generic-H6 class and gives a bijection on the 14,174-cell interior-force state space:

- the convex hull remains `0,1,2,3,4,5` after canonical relabeling;
- strict interior labels `6,7` remain interior;
- the missing relation graph is relabeled, so its type `C7` or `C3+C4` is preserved;
- reciprocal chirotope signs reverse orientation in the usual way under reflection;
- edge scalar signs stay attached to the relabeled edges;
- every exact local rank-two force condition is preserved.

Thus if a labelled generic-H6 cell is impossible, its reflected cell is impossible as well.

The later affine and branch conditions are also geometric and therefore reflection invariant. In particular, physical face pair `{2,3}` reflects to `{3,4}`. The ten admissible strict pentagon gap orders form one dihedral orbit, and the low/high median branches and rank-specific secants are permuted under reversal. Hence every committed exact Farkas exclusion has a reflected exact exclusion, even when that reflected cell has not yet been entered in an explicit candidate list.

## Ground-pattern action

At ground vertex `0`, reflection reverses the seven-entry CCW radial order. A normalized positive-position pattern

\[
P\subset\{1,\ldots,7\}
\]

therefore maps to

\[
\rho_P(P)=\{8-p:p\in P\}.
\]

On the surviving pattern names:

```text
145 <-> 347
156 <-> 237
235 <-> 356
236 <-> 256
245 <-> 346
345 <-> 345
```

